x491 text "primer"
x492 puts x490 x491
x493 call open x492 11
x494 write x493 2
x495 text "The primer"
x496 puts x494 x495
x497 call close x496 
x498 call open x497 2
x499 write x498 2
x500 text "This is everything a model is told before it writes or edits A0. The sections below say the same thing in full."
x501 puts x499 x500
x502 call close x501 
x503 call open x502 10
x504 write x503 4
x505 write x504 2
x506 text "code wrap"
x507 puts x505 x506
x508 call open x507 4
x509 write x508 2
x510 text "A0: `fn NAME T... -> T`, lines `ID OP ARG...`, `ret ARG` (or `ret OP ARGS`), `end`. Types u32 bool io, arrays u32x4, records (u32,bool). Params p0 p1... Args: earlier ID, pN, u32 literal, true, false. `use \"file.a0\"` at top links a file. No forward refs or recursion; ops exact mod 2^32.\n"
x511 puts x509 x510
x512 write x511 2
x513 text "mov add sub mul | and or xor (u32 bitwise, or bool logical) | shl shr (count&31) | div (b=0: 4294967295) rem (b=0: a) | eq ne (u32 or bool) lt le gt ge (unsigned) -> bool | select c x y\n"
x514 puts x512 x513
x515 write x514 2
x516 text "call F a... (F earlier) | fold F n s a... state=s; i<n: state=F(state,i,a...) | loop P F n s a... stops when P(...) false\n"
x517 puts x515 x516
x518 write x517 2
x519 text "arr e... | rec e... | text \"s\" | get a i (i mod N) | set a i v | at r k | put r k v (values, no aliasing)\n"
x520 puts x518 x519
x521 write x520 2
x522 text "io: linear token, each value used once. read t->(u32,io) | write t v->io | puts t a->io\n"
x523 puts x521 x522
x524 write x523 2
x525 text "EDIT: reply bare edit lines (handle line optional when one e handle is shown). `id op ...` replaces or inserts before ret; `... @ other` inserts after other; `-id` deletes; `ret x`; `fn ...` block (end optional) adds/replaces a function; `-fn name` removes.\n"
x526 puts x524 x525
x527 write x526 2
x528 text "Example: fn affine u32 u32 u32 -> u32 / a mul p0 p1 / b add a p2 / ret b / end (one item per line).\n"
x529 puts x527 x528
x530 call close x529 
x531 call close x530 
x532 call close x531 
x533 call open x532 13
x534 write x533 4
x535 write x534 1
x536 text "programs"
x537 puts x535 x536
x538 call open x537 11
x539 write x538 2
x540 text "Programs and functions"
x541 puts x539 x540
x542 call close x541 
x543 call open x542 2
x544 write x543 2
x545 text "A program is a list of functions. A function is a header `fn NAME T... -> T`, then one instruction per line `ID OP ARGS`, then `ret ARG` (or `ret OP ARGS`, which names a fresh node), then `end`. Names are lowercase identifiers. Parameters are p0, p1, ... in header order. An argument is an earlier ID in the same function, a parameter, a u32 literal, true, or false. There are no forward references, no recursion, and no nested expressions."
x546 puts x544 x545
x547 call close x546 
x548 call open x547 10
x549 write x548 4
x550 write x549 2
x551 text "code"
x552 puts x550 x551
x553 call open x552 4
x554 call open x553 6
x555 write x554 4
x556 write x555 2
x557 text "cm"
x558 puts x556 x557
x559 write x558 2
x560 text "# clamp p0 into [p1, p2]\n"
x561 puts x559 x560
x562 call close x561 
x563 write x562 2
x564 text "fn clamp u32 u32 u32 -> u32\nlo lt p0 p1\nhi lt p2 p0\na select lo p1 p0\nr select hi p2 a\nret r\nend"
x565 puts x563 x564
x566 call close x565 
x567 call close x566 
x568 call close x567 
x569 call open x568 13
x570 write x569 4
x571 write x570 1
x572 text "types"
x573 puts x571 x572
x574 call open x573 11
x575 write x574 2
x576 text "Types and values"
x577 puts x575 x576
x578 call close x577 
x579 call open x578 2
x580 write x579 2
x581 text "u32 is an exact 32-bit unsigned integer; every arithmetic result wraps modulo 2^32. bool is true or false, never a number. Arrays u32xN and records (T,T,...) are values: get, set, at, and put return a copy, they never alias. io is a linear token, meaning every io value is used exactly once; that is what makes output order checkable."
x582 puts x580 x581
x583 call close x582 
x584 call close x583 
x585 call open x584 13
x586 write x585 4
x587 write x586 1
x588 text "iteration"
x589 puts x587 x588
x590 call open x589 11
x591 write x590 2
x592 text "Iteration"
x593 puts x591 x592
x594 call close x593 
x595 call open x594 2
x596 write x595 2
x597 text "A function body has no loops. Repetition is fold and loop over an earlier function: the step function receives the state, the index, and any extra arguments, and returns the next state. loop adds a predicate function that is checked before each iteration. A literal count is checked against a per-function budget when the program is checked. A variable count is bounded by fuel (a step budget) in the reference interpreter, the plain slow implementation that every target is compared with; compiled targets have no execution budget."
x598 puts x596 x597
x599 call close x598 
x600 call open x599 10
x601 write x600 4
x602 write x601 2
x603 text "code"
x604 puts x602 x603
x605 call open x604 4
x606 call open x605 6
x607 write x606 4
x608 write x607 2
x609 text "cm"
x610 puts x608 x609
x611 write x610 2
x612 text "# sum of squares 0..n-1 with fold; the step is an earlier function\n"
x613 puts x611 x612
x614 call close x613 
x615 write x614 2
x616 text "fn sqstep u32 u32 -> u32\ns mul p1 p1\nr add p0 s\nret r\nend\nfn sumsq -> u32\nr fold sqstep 10 0\nret r\nend"
x617 puts x615 x616
x618 call close x617 
x619 call close x618 
x620 call close x619 
x621 call open x620 13
x622 write x621 4
x623 write x622 1
x624 text "modules"
x625 puts x623 x624
x626 call open x625 11
x627 write x626 2
x628 text "Modules"
x629 puts x627 x628
x630 call close x629 
x631 call open x630 2
x632 write x631 2
x633 text "A file starts with zero or more `use \"path.a0\"` lines, relative to the file. The linker loads every used file once, orders them by dependency, and checks the result as one program with one namespace. Cycles and duplicate function names are rejected, and diagnostics name the file and line."
x634 puts x632 x633
x635 call close x634 
x636 call open x635 10
x637 write x636 4
x638 write x637 2
x639 text "code"
x640 puts x638 x639
x641 call open x640 4
x642 write x641 2
x643 text "use \"ui.a0\"\nuse \"../examples/life.a0\"\nfn page io -> io\na call open p0 5\nb call close a\nret b\nend"
x644 puts x642 x643
x645 call close x644 
x646 call close x645 
x647 call close x646 
ret x647
end

