x654 call open x653 11
x655 write x654 2
x656 text "Views and edits"
x657 puts x655 x656
x658 call close x657 
x659 call open x658 2
x660 write x659 2
x661 text "A model never sees a whole file. It asks for a view of one function: the function with a handle line on top (e0), one signature line per callee, and a program handle (g0). The program view is scoped to the target, its transitive callees and its direct callers, so it stays the same size as the program grows. The revision is a short hash of the program text; an edit written against an older revision is rejected rather than applied to code that has moved. A reply is the handle line followed by edits, one per line, as in the quick start."
x662 puts x660 x661
x663 call close x662 
x664 call open x663 10
x665 write x664 4
x666 write x665 2
